{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/integrations/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T12:49:30.700297Z","id":"2b7c0ae2eb3a1c1256b44df3c8d4df58fb94ddb317d874e5471b2c46f44ce462","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/router.rs wrap() matches the reporter routes in front of every credential and host layer, so queue_reporter::router(state) is today what an outside backend's POST /api/queues/<qid>/reporter-tokens reaches. A layer wrap() later puts in front of those routes (a rate limit, a host check) would apply over HTTP and not to this in-process call, and the integration would stop being the exact outside path that docs/prod.md and the module docs describe. The test crates/clax-server/tests/api_feedback_integration.rs token_is_minted_through_the_public_route compares audit rows only.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":337},"end":{"line":338},"content_hash":"503672e02c587015bfaeada13313bb9a3f27c0fa4fb77917234a987000d47e9f"},"suggested_fix":"Hand the token route the instance's whole router (built once into AppState, or a OnceLock in the integration) instead of the reporter router.","summary":"The in-process mint goes to queue_reporter::router alone, not through the router wrap() builds","tags":["feedback","fidelity","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/integrations/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T14:18:00.622082Z","id":"31ae07bbe9c9e518fc368be5b78626d5e417b72f50cdeb719d8ca62a98b5e861","body":{"detail":"A flagged person's browser may mint reporter tokens as often as it sends the request; each mint is a row in queue_reporter_tokens (crates/clax-store/src/queues.rs mint_reporter_token), expired ones deleted a day after expiry. The public route's only bound is the agent gate's body allowance per signing key (crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs Gate), which here is the service grant's key shared by every person, so one person's burst can 429 everyone's mint. The codebase has no rate limiter with an injectable clock to reuse: clax_http::bot::ViewLimiter admits once per window, too strict for a token the shell renews.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":393},"end":{"line":420},"content_hash":"d0450bb730b7771d0f21e761116214539169dc736becddbe12e7646e822a3c99"},"suggested_fix":"A small per-person token bucket keyed by public ID, reading Store::now, in the handler before mint_request; or reuse a minted token until near its expires_at in the shell.","summary":"POST /_app/feedback/token has no per-person mint throttle","tags":["feedback","rate-limit","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/integrations/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T14:20:52.642124Z","id":"72bde2bf8d3e2b9c7532e52a7db68a094644868eb1626f68bd0e8a1c1ca2aae8","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:2f70026a6","summary":"token now mints through Instance::router (crates/clax-server/src/integrations/instance.rs): the router build_router makes, built once, with the Host the request signs. Evidence: bazel test //crates/clax-server:integration__3 PASSED, including api_feedback_integration::the_in_process_mint_is_the_public_routes_request (the same signed request replayed over HTTP answers 401 replayed_request) and a_revoked_grant_is_unavailable.","supersedes":"2b7c0ae2eb3a1c1256b44df3c8d4df58fb94ddb317d874e5471b2c46f44ce462","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/integrations/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T17:44:36.357258Z","id":"d475e5f2f6c47e21f2aa474ec708f241ab2146eb206631cb16bd23e9daf076d9","body":{"detail":"The token route copies a 429 and its Retry-After from the reporter-tokens route to the browser; crates/clax-server/tests/api_feedback_integration.rs tests the 400 invalid_key passthrough and the 503 for other refusals, but no test reaches the grant's nonce limit (QUEUE_NONCES_PER_KEY) through it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":440},"end":{"line":456},"content_hash":"bd850a6c5041600166fdf093c118e6e283112755ddd5b460ef6c4c3cb6ae626d"},"suggested_fix":"Drive the grant key past its limit with an injected clock (or a lowered limit) and assert 429 with Retry-After.","summary":"No test passes a 429 limit_reached from the public mint route back through POST /_app/feedback/token","tags":["feedback","test-gap","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
